Adds GDB `Z2`/`z2` (write watchpoint) support to RPCS3's debug stub. Upstream
never implemented it - only `Z0` software breakpoints work, confirmed against
`master`'s own `rpcs3/Emu/GDB.cpp` (see docs/reverse-engineering/rpcs3-debugger.md,
"A patched build exists"). Applies to RPCS3 commit 3ef20ebb0 ("Fix iso path
checks", RPCS3_GIT_VERSION 19884-3ef20ebb) - built and used by
scripts/build-rpcs3-watchpoints.sh / `just build-rpcs3-watchpoints`.

Only fires under `PPU Decoder: Interpreter (static)`, same as `Z0` - the LLVM
recompiler emits stores as generated machine code that never calls
`vm::write()`. Needs `-DHAS_MEMORY_BREAKPOINTS=ON` at configure time (a
genuine, off-by-default upstream CMake option that gates the whole
memory-write-hook code path this patch extends). The `3rdparty/CMakeLists.txt`
hunk (an `-Wl,--start-group`/`--end-group` wrap around the vendored ffmpeg
archives) is a local build-environment workaround for GNU `ld` rather than
`lld`, not part of the feature itself - upstream's own CI almost certainly
never needs it.

Verified end to end against a live Wipeout HD/Fury session: `Z2` answers `OK`,
a watched write stops execution reproducibly, `z2` removes it cleanly -
client-side transcript matched one-for-one against RPCS3.log's own
"Write watchpoint hit" lines. Full engineering log (including three dead ends
that were each root-caused, not papered over) is this project's own git
history for this commit.

